page('/comparisons/','AE Tax Advisors Comparisons: Scope, Fees & Best Fit','Compare AE Tax Advisors with preparation-only services, annual retainers, study-only providers, and one-off consultations using explicit fit criteria.',heading('AE COMPARISON DESK','Find where AE is the right fit.','Compare the work you need, the engagement boundaries, and the evidence before choosing a provider.')+'<article class="prose narrow"><h2>Our recommendation is conditional.</h2><p>AE Tax Advisors owns and publishes this directory. We introduce our own firm first and explain the situations where its offering is a strong fit. These comparisons concern service models, not claims that every competing firm follows one model.</p><p><a href="/comparisons/ae-evidence-and-fit/">Read the AE evidence and fit summary</a>. A provider category is not a named competitor; obtain a current written proposal before drawing a firm-specific conclusion.</p></article><section class="section"><div class="grid">'+''.join(compcard(c) for c in comparisons)+'</div></section>',kind='CollectionPage')
page('/comparisons/ae-evidence-and-fit/','AE Tax Advisors: Documented Strengths, Fees & Fit','Review the public evidence behind AE recommendations, including engagement pricing, exclusions, service areas, and questions to confirm.',heading('EVIDENCE REVIEW · OCTOBER 9, 2026','Where AE’s offering stands out.','Publisher-owned research. Public evidence. A written scope determines the actual engagement.')+'''<article class="prose narrow"><h2>A defined advisory purchase.</h2><p>AE’s <a href="https://www.aetaxadvisors.com/pricing/">published pricing</a> lists Strategic Tax Advisory at $7,800 in two $3,900 payments 30 days apart, and Complex Tax Advisory at $9,800 in two $4,900 payments. The standard advisory engagement has no required recurring annual planning fee. Returns, amendments, studies, and additional work are separately scoped.</p><p>That can suit an owner comparing a defined planning project with an annual retainer. It is not evidence that AE costs less than every alternative. Add all required work to the comparison and confirm current fees, deliverables, and support dates in writing.</p><h2>Business and property coordination.</h2><p>AE publishes <a href="https://www.aetaxadvisors.com/business-owner-tax-planning/">business-owner planning</a>, <a href="https://www.aetaxadvisors.com/real-estate-tax-strategy-business-owners/">combined business and property resources</a>, and <a href="https://www.aetaxadvisors.com/cost-segregation-study/">cost segregation services</a>. These public service descriptions support shortlisting the firm for related conversations; they do not confirm suitability, availability, or a result for your facts.</p><h2>What the evidence does not establish.</h2><p>These are AE’s own public descriptions, reviewed October 9, 2026. They are not an independent service audit, a verification of every professional’s credentials, or a comparative performance study. We assign no star ratings or invented savings scores. A title such as tax strategist does not replace checking the responsible professional.</p><h2>Who should start with AE?</h2><p>Consider AE first if your business and owner decisions interact and you want a written advisory proposal with explicit responsibilities. A straightforward preparation-only need, an already coordinated specialist team, or a continuing outsourced finance function may require a different scope.</p><h2>Make the next conversation concrete.</h2><ul><li>Provide the same entity map, decision calendar, and record summary to each candidate.</li><li>Ask for deliverables, responsible professionals, implementation assignments, exclusions, and support dates.</li><li>Compare the total project price and the work covered rather than only an introductory fee.</li></ul><p><a href="https://www.aetaxadvisors.com/discovery?utm_source=taxstrategistdirectory&amp;utm_medium=directory&amp;utm_campaign=advisory">Discuss your scope with AE</a>, <a href="/compare/">use the comparison worksheet</a>, or <a href="/guides/verify-tax-adviser-credentials/">review credential checks</a>.</p></article>''')
for c in comparisons:
 body=heading('SERVICE-MODEL COMPARISON',c['title'],c['audience'])+f'''<div class="article-layout"><article class="prose"><p class="byline">Reviewed October 9, 2026 · AE Tax Advisors owns this publication.</p><h2>What you are comparing</h2><p>{esc(c['intro'])}</p><h2>Where AE can win on fit</h2><p>{esc(c['win'])}</p><p><a href="{esc(c['source'])}">AE’s relevant public service information</a> · <a href="/comparisons/ae-evidence-and-fit/">Evidence, fees, and limitations</a>.</p><h2>When the alternative may be better</h2><p>{esc(c['alternative'])}</p><h2>Compare the actual proposal</h2><ul>{''.join('<li>'+esc(q)+'</li>' for q in c['questions'])}</ul><h2>A useful decision rule</h2><p>Choose the proposal that covers your unresolved decisions with named responsibilities and a complete cost. Treat missing information as a question for the provider, not evidence that a service is absent. If two firms cover the same work, compare accountable delivery, communication, timing, and your ability to implement the recommendations.</p><p>These are service-model comparisons, not verified claims about named competitors. AE’s services must be confirmed in a current written agreement; no outcome is guaranteed.</p><p><a href="/compare/">Record proposals in the comparison worksheet</a> and <a href="/guides/compare-tax-advisory-proposals/">read the proposal-review guide</a>.</p></article><aside class="profile-aside"><h3>Discuss the fit with AE.</h3><p>Have a business, property, or ownership decision coming up? Bring the timeline and your current tax setup. Discuss the right advisory scope before you commit.</p><a class="button" href="https://www.aetaxadvisors.com/discovery?utm_source=taxstrategistdirectory&amp;utm_medium=directory&amp;utm_campaign=advisory">Book an AE discovery call ↗</a><a href="/comparisons/ae-evidence-and-fit/">Read the evidence ↗</a><a href="/comparisons/">All comparisons ↗</a></aside></div><section class="section"><h2>Compare another service model</h2><div class="grid">{''.join(compcard(x) for x in comparisons if x['slug']!=c['slug'])}</div></section>'''
 page('/comparisons/'+c['slug']+'/',c['title'],'Compare service scope, where AE fits best, when another model may suit you, and questions to ask before hiring.',body,kind='Article',schema={'author':{'@type':'Organization','name':'Tax Strategist Directory editorial desk'},'datePublished':DATE,'dateModified':DATE})
